SECTION C — PARITY NOTES (web source is THE specification)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
C1. Behaviour reproduced 1:1 from RouteAnnouncer.tsx — all of the web component's real branches:
      • first-render guard — the initial route is recorded as the baseline and NEVER announced
        (web `if (firstRender.current) return;` — the browser already speaks the title on load).
      • deferred read — each subsequent route schedules a `delayMs` (default 100 ms) read through the
        RouteAnnounceScheduler seam (web `window.setTimeout`); nothing settles before the clock fires.
      • cancel-pending — a newer route cancels the prior pending read (web effect-cleanup
        `clearTimeout`), so rapid navigation announces only the final destination.
      • empty-title clear — an empty settled title clears the region and posts nothing, WITHOUT
        burning a rotation (web `if (!title) { setMessage(''); return; }` returns before the counter).
      • dedup rotation — a rotating 0–3 U+200B suffix (web `counter.current = (counter.current+1)%4;
        '\u200B'.repeat(counter.current)`) so two consecutive routes with the SAME title both
        re-announce. Own inline padding (RouteAnnouncementPadding), NOT the sibling AnnouncerPadding —
        faithful to the web file keeping its OWN counter separate from useAnnouncer.
C2. States: the prompt mandates "every state MUST render — no hidden surfaces". Following the COMMITTED
    sibling AnnouncerRegion (P4-0001, also an anonymous a11y surface), this is a VISIBLE route-
    announcement inspector that renders loading / empty / error / data + the stale/offline freshness
    chip, while performing the REAL assistive-tech voicing through the presenter seam. The web hidden
    region maps to a static visible region card (never double-spoken) + the imperative
    AccessibilityNotification.Announcement at .default (polite) speech priority — the iOS 18 / macOS 15
    route-change idiom; route changes are always polite (web `priority="polite"`).
C3. Data sources: bound to the navigation feed via the P1/S8 RouteAnnouncerSource seam (the native
    `useLocation` peer = LiveRouteAnnouncerSource, mounted once like the web `<App/>`). The web source
    DELIBERATELY does not route through useAnnouncer (it documents why — route changes are declarative
    and own their region); the native port mirrors that with its own RouteAnnouncementPresenter rather
    than the shared Announcer. The prompt's auto-listed "useAnnouncer" is superseded by the actual
    source, exactly as the web file states.
C4. i18n (P1/S10): table "RouteAnnouncer", 19 keys, no English literal in code (every Text resolves
    through RouteAnnouncerStrings). Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened emitted once with surface slug
    "RouteAnnouncer". Accessibility: VoiceOver region/history labels (asserted by test), Dynamic Type
    semantic fonts, reduce-motion respected (TSFadeIn honours it), no neon body text, no raw HTML/hex.

